## Code Snippets — Mandatory `impl-tabs` Rule

**Every fenced `java` or `go` implementation snippet in a system-design post must use `impl-tabs`.** These appear in §6 Core Algorithms, low-level subsections, or interface sketches — never as raw vertical Java-only blocks.

### When to use `impl-tabs`

| Content type | Use `impl-tabs`? | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Java / Go class or interface sketches | **Yes — required** | §6 algorithms, connection registries, Lua-adjacent Java, etc. |
| Multiple related snippets in one subsection | **Yes** | All Java in `lang="java"` tab; all Go in `lang="golang"` tab |
| JSON in API shortcodes (`api-request` / `api-response`) | **No** | API §3 keeps existing shortcodes |
| Mermaid / ASCII diagrams | **No** | Unchanged |
| SQL, Redis CLI, shell one-liners | **No** | Single fence is fine |

### When NOT to use (forbidden)

| Do NOT | Why |
|---|---|
| Bare ` ```java` under a `###` heading | Stacks code without Go parity; page grows vertically |
| `### Java` / `### Go` split headings | Use horizontal tabs instead |
| `{< impl-tabs >}` (single brace) | Hugo will not parse — use `{{< >}}` |

### Canonical template

```markdown
### Connection Registry (Low-Level)

{{< impl-tabs default="java" java="Java" golang="Go" >}}
{{< impl-tab lang="java" >}}

```java
public class ConnectionRegistryRepository implements ChatConnectionManager {
    // ...
}
```

{{< /impl-tab >}}
{{< impl-tab lang="golang" >}}

```go
type ConnectionRegistry struct {
    // idiomatic Go equivalent
}
```

{{< /impl-tab >}}
{{< /impl-tabs >}}
```

### Shortcode contract

| Shortcode | Required params |
|---|---|
| `impl-tabs` | `default="java"`, `java="Java"`, `golang="Go"` |
| `impl-tab` | `lang="java"` or `lang="golang"` |

- Use `{{<` / `>}}` delimiters when panels contain fenced code.
- Java tab first (default); Go second.
- Replace `// TODO` Go stubs with real implementations when editing a post.

Bulk migration: `python scripts/migrate_system_design_code_tabs.py` wraps existing ` ```java` fences.

