## API & Request Flows — Prefer Sequence Diagrams

After **§5 High-Level Architecture** (`flowchart LR`), path subsections must use **`sequenceDiagram`** — not numbered prose steps and not `flowchart TD` for multi-service request choreography.

### Diagram type selection (canonical)

| Layer | Mermaid type | Use when |
|---|---|---|
| **§5 HLD** | `flowchart LR` | Static topology — components and data stores |
| **§5 path subsections** | `sequenceDiagram` | Request Evaluation, Read/Write paths, Ingestion/Delivery, Admin config |
| **§6 algorithms (in-process)** | `flowchart TD` | LRU steps, token refill logic, lock-striping inside one node |
| **§6 lifecycles** | `stateDiagram-v2` | Booking status, payment intent states |
| **Async pipelines (no return path)** | `flowchart LR` or `sequenceDiagram` with `--)` | Kafka → consumer → warehouse |

### Replace numbered lists with `sequenceDiagram` when

| Pattern in markdown | Convert to |
|---|---|
| `### Request Evaluation Path` + steps | `sequenceDiagram` with `alt` allow/deny |
| `### Read Path` / `### Write Path` | `sequenceDiagram` with `alt` cache hit/miss |
| `### Ingestion Path` / `### Delivery Path` | `sequenceDiagram` |
| `### Payment Confirmation` | `sequenceDiagram` |
| `### Admin Configuration Path` | `sequenceDiagram` |
| `**Estimation path:** A → B → C` one-liners | `sequenceDiagram` or `flowchart LR` |

Use Mermaid `alt` / `opt` / `par` blocks for branches (allowed vs 429, cache hit vs miss, fail-open).

### Keep as text (do not diagram)

| Content | Why |
|---|---|
| §3 API Design overview table + `api-endpoint` shortcodes | Contract reference |
| Component responsibility tables | Not a temporal flow |
| Cache sizing / capacity math | Numbers, not choreography |
| §6 class diagrams | Structure, not request path |

### Canonical path subsection (reference: `distributed-rate-limiter.md`, `urlshortner.md` §5)

```markdown
### Request Evaluation Path

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant Envoy as API Gateway
    participant RL as Rate Limiter
    participant Redis as Redis Cluster
    participant App as Downstream Services

    Client->>Envoy: HTTPS request
    Envoy->>RL: evaluate rules
    RL->>Redis: Lua EVAL (atomic)
    Redis-->>RL: tokens remaining
    alt allowed
        RL->>App: forward
        App-->>Client: 200 OK
    else denied
        RL-->>Client: 429 + Retry-After
    end
```
```

One optional sentence below the diagram for trade-offs — **do not** duplicate steps in a numbered list.

### Sequence diagram conventions

| Do | Avoid |
|---|---|
| `participant Redis as Redis Cluster` aliases for long names | Ambiguous participant IDs (`Redis` as sole ID when multiple caches exist) |
| `alt` / `opt` for branches | Separate flowchart TD for the same request path |
| `-->>` sync replies; `--)` async fire-and-forget | Blocking analytics on the hot-path arrow |
| Keep 4–8 participants per diagram | 12+ participants — split into two diagrams |

