## Mermaid Rules (v11)

| Do | Avoid |
|----|-------|
| Quote edge labels: `\|"GET /v1/resource"\|` | `\n` in unquoted labels |
| `participant X as Display Name` in sequence diagrams | Reserved/special chars in participant aliases |
| `alt` / `opt` / `par` blocks in `sequenceDiagram` | Duplicating the same path as `flowchart TD` under §5 |
| Curly braces in labels: `{code}` | Ambiguous IDs like `Redis`, `Kafka` as sole node names |
| Use `<br/>` for line breaks in nodes | Ambiguous IDs like `Redis`, `Kafka` as node names |
| camelCase subgraph IDs: `subgraph readPath["Read Path"]` | Unquoted multi-line labels |
| Cylinder nodes: `[("PostgreSQL<br/>Primary")]` | Static images when Mermaid suffices |

**Required diagram types per post:**
- `erDiagram` — data model (§4)
- `flowchart LR` — high-level architecture (§5 HLD only)
- `sequenceDiagram` — read/write/ingest/delivery paths under §5 (required for multi-service flows)
- `flowchart TD` — in-process algorithms, scaling stages (§6–§7)
- `flowchart LR` — optional for linear async pipelines (analytics fire-and-forget)
- `stateDiagram-v2` — optional for lifecycle state machines
- `classDiagram` — optional for strategy/adapter structure (§6)

## Workflow

1. Sketch in draw.io (requirements → API → schema → architecture → capacity)
2. Create `content/system-design/<name>.md` using the 11-section template
3. Convert diagrams to Mermaid (no static image unless Mermaid cannot express it)
4. Preview: `hugo server -D` — hard refresh (`Ctrl+Shift+R`) and verify checklist below
5. Set `draft: false` when ready to publish

### Preview checklist (every post)

| Check | Expected |
|-------|----------|
| §1–§11 headers | Bordered cards with **Expand** pill (§5 HLD always visible, no toggle) |
| §4 Data Model | `erDiagram` renders as SVG inside `.diagram-frame`; **Click to expand** fills modal (not tiny centered thumbnail) |
| §5 High-Level Architecture | `flowchart LR` renders as SVG; inline scrolls horizontally if wide; expand fills viewport |
| §5 path subsections | `sequenceDiagram` for request paths — not numbered step lists |
| API §3 | Overview table visible; endpoint panels collapse/expand |
| Standalone error codes | No bogus `h2` between §3 and §4 — use `{{% api-errors %}}` |
| Diagram lightbox | Reset/Fit re-centers diagram; scroll zooms; no console errors on expand |
| Code tabs | **Java** / **Go** buttons visible; Java default; Go click switches panel |
| Browser console | No `NotFoundError`, no uncaught DOM exceptions |

Spot-check reference posts: `urlshortner.md`, `distributed-rate-limiter.md`, `ticket-booking.md`.

## Writing Style

- Use markdown tables for requirements, calculations, comparisons, and capacity
- State concrete numbers (RPS, storage GB, pod counts) — never vague "lots of traffic"
- Separate read and write paths when the system is asymmetric
- Offload analytics/async work off the hot path (e.g. Kafka → analytics store)
- Name services by responsibility (e.g. Write Service vs Read Service), not generic "API"
